@page "/products/contracts"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Serga Contracts"; ViewData["Description"] = "Agreement lifecycle management with owners, obligations, documents, notice periods and renewals."; }
<section class="hero container detail-hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Serga Contracts</p><h1>Know what you’ve agreed to.<br /><em>And what happens next.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">Keep agreements, counterparties, owners, documents and deadlines together throughout the commercial lifecycle.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/platform">Explore the platform <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><partial name="_ContractsMockup" /></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">From scattered documents to shared context</p><h2>The agreement is only<br /><em>the beginning.</em></h2><p>A file in a shared drive cannot tell everyone who owns the next decision. Email, spreadsheets and individual knowledge leave obligations and dates disconnected.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>Agreement & counterparty</h3><p>Relate each agreement to its customer or supplier, owner and commercial value.</p></article><article><h3>Dates & decisions</h3><p>Keep start and end dates, notice periods, renewals and important dates in view.</p></article><article><h3>Documents & obligations</h3><p>Bring supporting documents and responsibilities alongside the terms they explain.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Example: a supplier renewal</p><h2>Before the deadline.<br /><em>Before the surprise.</em></h2><p>Control over the agreement lifecycle, with the commercial context needed to decide what happens next.</p></div><ol class="workflow"><li><span class="eyebrow">01</span><strong>Register the agreement</strong><p>Connect the supplier, owner, value and documents.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">02</span><strong>Identify commitments</strong><p>Capture obligations, notice periods and key dates.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">03</span><strong>Review what’s next</strong><p>Give the responsible owner the context to review renewal terms.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">04</span><strong>Record the decision</strong><p>Keep the outcome and updated agreement together.</p></li></ol></section>

<section class="context-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Independently useful. Better together.</p><h2>Clear agreements.<br /><em>Connected decisions.</em></h2><p>Use Contracts independently to organize agreements and obligations. Add other Serga products when the relationship calls for them.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>A home for commercial context</h3><p>Keep legal drafting in your existing process. Serga organizes what was agreed and the responsibilities that follow.</p></article><article><h3>Alongside your systems</h3><p>Relate agreements to customer and supplier records in the wider business. Integration depends on the systems involved.</p></article><article><h3>Optional shared context</h3><p>Connect an agreement to recurring customer revenue or leased equipment, without making either product a prerequisite.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Make the connection</p><h2>Stay ahead of<br /><em>what happens next.</em></h2><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span class="cta-tagline">Your gateway to services</span></div></section>
